<p><span class="body-text"><b>15 - Who wants to taste taste of the hidden light</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>[Language of our rabbi, of blessed memory] And you shall be to Me kingdom of priests etc. (Exodus 19)</b></span></p><p><span style="text-transform: uppercase"><span style="letter-spacing: 2.4pt"><b>1.</b></span></span></p><p><span class="body-text">Who wants to taste taste of the hidden light that is secrets of the Torah that will be revealed for the future needs to raise attribute of the&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;to its root.</span></p><p><span style="text-transform: uppercase"><span style="letter-spacing: 2.4pt"><b>2.</b></span></span></p><p><span class="body-text">And with what raise the&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">? in aspect of&nbsp;</span>judgment<span class="body-text">&nbsp;as written (Proverbs 29): &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>king in judgment establishes land</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; and land is aspect of&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;as written (Psalms 76): &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>land feared</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; that is that judge all his businesses as written (there 112): &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>sustains his words in judgment</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; that is that judge and judge in himself all his businesses and in this removes from upon him all the fears and raises aspect of&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;pure and clean and remains but fear of Hashem and not fear other because when no man judges and judges himself then judge and judge him above because if no judgment below there is judgment above (Devarim Rabba 5) and when judge the man in upper judgment then the judgment clothed in all the things and all the things made messengers to the Omnipresent to do in this the man&nbsp;</span>judgment<span class="body-text">&nbsp;written as our sages, of blessed memory, said (Nedarim 41). &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>to Your judgments they stood</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot;, then &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>all Your servants</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; to do judgment in this the man but when judges himself and when there is judgment below no judgment above and no the&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;clothed in any thing to arouse the man because he himself aroused and this (Psalms 50): &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>and places way</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; who places his ways (as our rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded Sotah 5:) that is that judges his ways as written (Exodus 21): &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>and these the judgments that you place</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; (see Genesis Rabba p 26 Mishpatim p 30) through this &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>I will show him in salvation of G-d</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; this aspect of&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;as written (Ecclesiastes 12): &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>G-d fear</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; that is aspect of&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;ascends from the klipah and from the nations through&nbsp;</span>judgment<span class="body-text">&nbsp;because from beginning was clothed in the klipah and this that the man fears himself from some thing from minister or from thieves and rest fears this that the&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;clothed in this the thing because if not was clothed the&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;in this the thing not was power in this the thing to frighten the man.</span></p><p><span style="text-transform: uppercase"><span style="letter-spacing: 2.4pt"><b>3.</b></span></span></p><p><span class="body-text">And root of the&nbsp;</span>fear<span class="body-text">&nbsp;is knowledge as written in Etz Chaim that mantzpak it in knowledge of small face a